jsoncpp: a range of policy versions in the installed jsoncppConfig.cmake instead of a bare 3.0.

The template jsoncppConfig.cmake.in (our pin 69098a18) starts with cmake_policy(VERSION 3.0). The consumer runs this
file on find_package(jsoncpp), here the configure of the SDK itself (cmake/Dependencies.cmake). CMake 4 removed the
compatibility with versions below 3.5 and fails on this line unless CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM is set. The range
3.0...3.24 is as in the exports CMake generates itself (jsoncpp-targets.cmake next to it): CMake before 3.12 reads it
as 3.0 (as before), newer ones take the policies of their version but not above 3.24; CMake 4 accepts it. The build of
jsoncpp is not affected: the template is only substituted by configure_package_config_file on install. Remove with a
pin bump if the new jsoncpp has the line fixed.

--- a/jsoncppConfig.cmake.in
+++ b/jsoncppConfig.cmake.in
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 cmake_policy(PUSH)
-cmake_policy(VERSION 3.0)
+cmake_policy(VERSION 3.0...3.24)
 
 @PACKAGE_INIT@
 
